(7699552, 1263386, 103142, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LevT:</b></div><hr/><i> Very nice image Wendy, congrats on your ribbon! For me, for this particular challenge, it lacked depth a little bit. I myself was searching for a shot that communicates a huge depth of field. I know that sky is vast and limitless, it''s just my visual impression that here it repesents a nice (but somewhat flat) background for the birds. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree with you, actually. I just didn''t have anything else that began to fit it. It was only when I saw that the birds were so far away, and yet so clear, that I thought that it might work for the challenge. I was quite surprised at the outcome!</td>', 'Originally posted by LevT: Very nice image Wendy, congrats on your ribbon! For me, for this particular challenge, it lacked depth a little bit. I myself was searching for a shot that communicates a huge depth of field. I know that sky is vast and limitless, it''s just my visual impression that here it repesents a nice (but somewhat flat) background for the birds.   I agree with you, actually. I just didn''t have anything else that began to fit it. It was only when I saw that the birds were so far away, and yet so clear, that I thought that it might work for the challenge. I was quite surprised at the outcome!', '2021-08-24 10:13:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(7699553, 1263154, 103142, '<td valign="top">This is amazing! What a fascinating place! (I''ve been out on vacation, so just catching up on things. I replied to your comment on mine. :)<br/> <br/>I need to study landscape photography more. None of my landscapes even remotely came across as "expanse". I think it''s because I miss the foreground elements, or something like that.<br/> <br/>This makes me want to go see Death Valley (ok, I already want to go for the night skies, but now I want to go even more. :)</td>', 'This is amazing! What a fascinating place! (I''ve been out on vacation, so just catching up on things. I replied to your comment on mine. :) I need to study landscape photography more. None of my landscapes even remotely came across as "expanse". I think it''s because I miss the foreground elements, or something like that. This makes me want to go see Death Valley (ok, I already want to go for the night skies, but now I want to go even more. :)', '2021-08-24 10:16:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(7727168, 1263336, 68504, '<td valign="top">this is really a triumph of colour. the saturation comment and response makes us take note of the natural UNsaturated sky. (I live by the sea, the light is always changing and what Ocean offers up is astonishing).</td>', 'this is really a triumph of colour. the saturation comment and response makes us take note of the natural UNsaturated sky. (I live by the sea, the light is always changing and what Ocean offers up is astonishing).', '2022-08-11 02:19:44.000000', NULL, 0);
